    "title": "Who is Jai Lucas? Miami basketball coach sparked record turnaround",
    "text": "HURRICANESJai Lucas brought stars to Duke. Now he's got Miami into March Madness Dan RorabaughUSA TODAY NETWORK - FloridaMarch 20, 2026Updated March 21, 2026, 2:05 p.m. ET(This story has been updated to reflect Miami beating Missouri in March Madness.)Miami might have known it struck gold when it hired Jai Lucas to be its men's basketball coach, but who would have thought he could turn the Hurricanes around this quickly?Lucas came to Coral Gables from a star-making turn as recruiting director and assistant coach at Duke. He replaced a legend in Jim Larrañaga, who led the 'Canes to the Final Four in 2023 but saw the program fall apart after that, leading him to resign amid a horrid 7-24 season in 2024.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
